# Remember these categories:
Category:	Main Services
Compute: 	EC2, Lambda, ECS, EKS, Fargate, Elastic Beanstalk
Storage:	S3, EBS, EFS, Glacier
Database:	RDS, DynamoDB, Aurora, Redshift
Networking:	VPC, ELB, Route 53, CloudFront, Direct Connect
Security:	IAM, WAF, Shield, KMS, Cognito
Monitoring:	CloudWatch, CloudTrail, Config, Trusted Advisor
DevOps:	CodeCommit, CodeBuild, CodeDeploy, CodePipeline, CloudFormation
Messaging:	SQS, SNS, EventBridge
Scaling: 	EC2 Auto Scaling, Application Auto Scaling

🖥️ Compute Services
1. Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)
Definition:
Amazon EC2 is a virtual server service that allows users to create and manage virtual machines (instances) in the cloud.
> Features
Launch virtual servers in minutes
Multiple operating systems (Linux, Windows)
Scalable computing power
Pay only for what you use
> Use Cases
Website hosting
Web applications
Game servers
Backend servers
2. AWS Lambda
Definition:
AWS Lambda is a serverless computing service that runs your code automatically in response to events without managing servers.
> Features
No server management
Automatic scaling
Pay only for execution time
Supports multiple programming languages
> Use Cases
Image processing
API backend
File uploads
Automation
3. AWS Elastic Beanstalk
Definition:
Elastic Beanstalk is a Platform as a Service (PaaS) that automatically deploys, manages, and scales web applications.
>Features
Easy deployment
Automatic scaling
Health monitoring
Supports Java, Python, Node.js, PHP, .NET
>Use Cases
Web application hosting
API deployment
4. Amazon ECS (Elastic Container Service)
Definition:
Amazon ECS is a fully managed container orchestration service used to run Docker containers.
>Features
Docker support
Easy container management
Auto scaling
Integrated with AWS services
>Use Cases
Microservices
Docker applications
5. Amazon EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service)
Definition:
Amazon EKS is a managed Kubernetes service that helps deploy and manage Kubernetes clusters.
>Features
Managed Kubernetes
High availability
Secure cluster management
Automatic updates
>Use Cases
Kubernetes applications
Enterprise container workloads
6. AWS Fargate
Definition:
AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers that eliminates the need to manage servers.
>Features
No EC2 management
Automatic scaling
Pay per resource usage
>Use Cases
Running Docker containers
Containerized applications
💾 Storage Services
1. Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service)

Definition:
Amazon S3 is an object storage service used to store unlimited amounts of files such as images, videos, backups, and documents.

Features

Highly durable
Secure storage
Versioning
Lifecycle management

Use Cases

Website hosting
File storage
Backup
Data archive
2. Amazon EBS (Elastic Block Store)

Definition:
Amazon EBS provides block-level storage volumes that are attached to EC2 instances.

Features

High performance
Persistent storage
Snapshots
SSD and HDD options

Use Cases

Operating system storage
Database storage
3. Amazon EFS (Elastic File System)

Definition:
Amazon EFS is a scalable shared file storage service that multiple EC2 instances can access simultaneously.

Features

Shared storage
Automatic scaling
High availability

Use Cases

Shared applications
Content management
4. Amazon S3 Glacier

Definition:
Amazon S3 Glacier is a low-cost storage service designed for long-term backup and data archiving.

Features

Very low storage cost
Secure archive
Long-term retention

Use Cases

Backup
Compliance storage
🗄️ Database Services
1. Amazon RDS (Relational Database Service)

Definition:
Amazon RDS is a managed relational database service that supports MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server, and MariaDB.

Features

Automated backups
High availability
Easy maintenance

Use Cases

Web applications
ERP systems
2. Amazon DynamoDB

Definition:
Amazon DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database designed for high-speed applications.

Features

Millisecond response
Automatic scaling
Serverless

Use Cases

Gaming
Mobile apps
IoT
3. Amazon Aurora

Definition:
Amazon Aurora is a high-performance relational database compatible with MySQL and PostgreSQL.

Features

Faster than MySQL
Highly available
Automatic backups

Use Cases

Enterprise applications
Banking systems
4. Amazon Redshift

Definition:
Amazon Redshift is a cloud data warehouse used for big data analytics.

Features

Fast analytics
SQL support
Massive storage

Use Cases

Business intelligence
Reporting
🌐 Networking & Content Delivery
1. Amazon VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)

Definition:
Amazon VPC allows users to create a private network within AWS.

Features

Private IP addresses
Subnets
Route tables
Security Groups

Use Cases

Secure cloud infrastructure
2. Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)

Definition:
Elastic Load Balancing distributes incoming traffic across multiple servers.

Features

High availability
Automatic traffic distribution
Fault tolerance

Use Cases

High-traffic websites
3. Amazon Route 53

Definition:
Amazon Route 53 is AWS's DNS service that routes users to applications.

Features

Domain registration
Health checks
Traffic routing

Use Cases

Website domain management
4. Amazon CloudFront

Definition:
Amazon CloudFront is a Content Delivery Network (CDN) that delivers content from the nearest edge location.

Features

Faster content delivery
Global edge locations
Security

Use Cases

Video streaming
Website acceleration
5. AWS Direct Connect

Definition:
AWS Direct Connect provides a dedicated private network connection between your data center and AWS.

Features

High bandwidth
Low latency
Secure connection

Use Cases

Enterprise networking
🔐 Security & Identity
1. AWS IAM (Identity and Access Management)

Definition:
IAM controls who can access AWS resources and what actions they can perform.

Features

Users
Groups
Roles
Policies

Use Cases

Access control
2. AWS Shield

Definition:
AWS Shield protects applications from DDoS attacks.

Features

Automatic protection
Network security
3. AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall)

Definition:
AWS WAF protects web applications from common web attacks like SQL Injection and Cross-Site Scripting (XSS).

Features

Rule-based filtering
Traffic monitoring
4. AWS KMS (Key Management Service)

Definition:
AWS KMS is used to create and manage encryption keys for securing AWS data.

Features

Encryption
Secure key management
5. AWS Cognito

Definition:
AWS Cognito provides user authentication, authorization, and user management for applications.

Features

User Sign-up
Sign-in
Social login
Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
📊 Monitoring & Management
1. Amazon CloudWatch

Definition:
CloudWatch monitors AWS resources and applications by collecting logs, metrics, and events.

Features

Monitoring
Alerts
Dashboards
2. AWS CloudTrail

Definition:
CloudTrail records all API calls and user activities performed in an AWS account.

Features

Audit logs
Security tracking
3. AWS Config

Definition:
AWS Config tracks and records the configuration of AWS resources.

Features

Configuration history
Compliance checking
4. AWS Trusted Advisor

Definition:
Trusted Advisor analyzes your AWS environment and provides recommendations to improve security, performance, cost optimization, and reliability.

Features

Cost optimization
Security checks
Performance recommendations
⚙️ DevOps & Deployment
1. AWS CodeCommit

Definition:
A fully managed Git repository service for storing and managing source code.

2. AWS CodeBuild

Definition:
A fully managed build service that compiles source code, runs tests, and creates deployment packages.

3. AWS CodeDeploy

Definition:
Automates application deployment to EC2 instances, Lambda functions, and on-premises servers.

4. AWS CodePipeline

Definition:
A Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) service that automates the software release process.

5. AWS CloudFormation

Definition:
An Infrastructure as Code (IaC) service that provisions AWS resources using templates.

📩 Messaging & Integration
1. Amazon SQS (Simple Queue Service)

Definition:
A message queue service that enables different applications or services to communicate asynchronously.

Use Case
Order processing, background jobs.

2. Amazon SNS (Simple Notification Service)

Definition:
A publish/subscribe messaging service used to send notifications to multiple subscribers.

Use Case
SMS alerts, email notifications.

3. Amazon EventBridge
An event bus service that connects applications using events and triggers automated workflows.
>Use Case
Automation, event-driven architectures.

📈 Scaling & Load Management
1. Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling
Automatically increases or decreases the number of EC2 instances based on demand.
> Benefits
Saves cost
Maintains performance
Handles traffic spikes

2. AWS Application Auto Scaling
Automatically scales AWS services such as DynamoDB, ECS, Aurora, Lambda Provisioned Concurrency, and others based on usage.
>Benefits
Automatic scaling
Improved availability
Cost optimization